PSCI SYSTEM_RESET failsafe for the scheduled reboot + crash-report dumper.

FEATURE A - reliable reset (fixes the hang after "launchd quiesce complete"):
  reboot_kernel() -> halt_all_cpus(TRUE) -> PEHaltRestart(kPERestartCPU)
  and PE_halt_restart is NULL on this platform, so the device never resets.
  The SMC conduit is known good (patch 0065's PSCI CPU_ON), so add:
    - sweet_psci_system_reset(): x0 = 0x84000009 (PSCI SYSTEM_RESET), "smc #0"
      with the same clobbers as sweet_psci_cpu_on() (0065 SweetCPU.cpp);
    - `sweetrebootat=<secs>` now prints "SWEET REBOOT: firing now", starts a
      45 s failsafe kernel thread that calls sweet_psci_system_reset(), and
      still calls reboot_kernel(RB_AUTOBOOT, "sweetrebootat") as before;
    - new `sweetpscireset=<secs>` (default off): sleep N s and call
      sweet_psci_system_reset() directly - the fast hardware validation path.
  Banners: "SWEET RESET: armed for N s" / "SWEET RESET: PSCI SYSTEM_RESET".

FEATURE B - crash-report dumper (SpringBoard SIGABRT needs its .ips report):
  `sweetdumptree=<dir>[,<dir>...]` (default off) after
  `sweetdumptreetime` s (default 120) lists each directory with VNOP_READDIR
  (kernel 32-bit-ino struct dirent) and prints one line per entry:
    TREE <dir> entry=<name> type=<d_type> size=<size>
    TREE <dir> err=<errno>                     (directory missing)
  then dumps the text of regular files whose name ends in
  `sweetdumptreeext` (default "ips"):
    CRASHFILE <path> size=<n>
    CF| <line>                                 (<=200 chars/line, non-printables '.')
    CRASHFILE end <path>
  The total CF output is bounded by `sweetdumptreemax` (default 524288 bytes);
  at most 4 directories and 200 entries per directory are processed.

Both features are boot-arg gated and started from the same place as the other
SWEET threads (onc_emmc extras / sweet_sample_start); without the boot args
nothing changes.  Files: bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c (feature B) and
bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c (feature A + starting the dumper).
